('1a768d5f-a2b6-51c0-9432-ac2f5fa40188'::uuid, $dq$["injury"]$dq$::jsonb, $dq$medium$dq$, '2026-04-11'::date, '11:00'::time, 'b01b0bb1-b2f3-5276-aea0-4be1186d18ab'::uuid, $dq$Naustavör$dq$, NULL, $dq$$dq$, $dq$While rearranging keelboats in the parking lot, a club member rolled the front left wheel of Gróa over his two large right toes, wearing only neoprene booties. The big toe was split lengthwise on the medial side ("like a burst pylsa") and the nail of the second toe was crushed.$dq$, $dq$Þorsteinn$dq$, $dq$Steve, Orri, Hannes, Árni, Lara, Guðjón, others$dq$, $dq$SDS exposed, applied direct pressure. Then irrigated with drinking water, examined, continued pressure, and bandaged. Randi came to drive him to Slýsó for cleaning, suturing, evaluation.$dq$, $dq$None. SDS called ÞA just before k. 15 to check in. All good. Tx included imaging for break/fracture.$dq$, $dq$other$dq$, $dq$Randi$dq$, $dq$none$dq$, ARRAY[]::text[], $dq$steve$dq$, '2026-04-11T15:06:09.496Z'::timestamptz, true, '2026-04-11T15:06:09.496Z'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, $dq$closed$dq$),
('d5db30af-4367-59ba-bbd9-aa2e395e0696'::uuid, $dq$["capsize", "propertyDmg", "equipment"]$dq$::jsonb, $dq$medium$dq$, '2026-04-19'::date, '14:00'::time, '9a0b7ef4-e0cc-5ab7-84e3-104a59e051b4'::uuid, $dq$Fossvogur$dq$, '5c8df410-1369-51dd-b54b-1b898c280af3'::uuid, $dq$Topaz Argo$dq$, $dq$See scout log for details. Argo was launched in heavy wind without strap to fix rudder vertically. Crew had difficulty maneouvering. Before ability to head to harbor, capsized into mud. During recovery, mast head snapped. Hull was clipped by prammi motor; prop & hull chipped. Boom gooseneck snapped when derigging. Neighbors had alerted EMS/police. SDS spoke to them ca. 14:45 with no follow up. One scout not in wetsuit, but$dq$, $dq$SDS, scouts (see abler), Ali$dq$, $dq$$dq$, $dq$Recovered Argo to ramp$dq$, $dq$Repairs; check in with scouts.$dq$, $dq$$dq$, $dq$$dq$, $dq$$dq$, ARRAY[]::text[], $dq$steve$dq$, '2026-04-20T11:53:08.291Z'::timestamptz, true, '2026-04-20T11:57:02.163Z'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, $dq$closed$dq$),
('7ff59722-3b40-50d4-9f9f-c45b3fad193b'::uuid, $dq$["nearMiss", "propertyDmg"]$dq$::jsonb, $dq$medium$dq$, '2026-05-03'::date, '14:30'::time, 'b01b0bb1-b2f3-5276-aea0-4be1186d18ab'::uuid, $dq$Naustavör$dq$, '15f72153-65d1-584d-b21c-318d3ba08847'::uuid, $dq$Quest 1$dq$, $dq$Bjarki +1 arrived to sail, unarranged. Quest had been used in the morning for scouts, was at dock. Evidently plug had not been in: last use had been SÍL þjálfaranámskeið. Plug had been set in rudder hole. SDS directed Bjarki to ramp on discovery, stayed with scouts. Alli, Gunnar S. aided with draining by pulling waterlogged boat up ramp with jeep. Snapped several lines, broke trolley head at weld. Sailing fine afterward. Boat kept at dock overnight.$dq$, $dq$Bjarki Freyr, +1, Alli, Gunnar S., (SDS/Viktor in AM).$dq$, $dq$$dq$, $dq$Alli contacted son re: weld options.$dq$, $dq$Trolley needs repair$dq$, $dq$$dq$, $dq$$dq$, $dq$$dq$, ARRAY[]::text[], $dq$steve$dq$, '2026-05-04T02:23:58.525Z'::timestamptz, true, '2026-05-16T15:36:47.506Z'::timestamptz, NULL, $dq$[{"by":"steve","at":"2026-05-16T15:36:44.832Z","text":"Palli welded, SDS zincked"}]$dq$, $dq$closed$dq$),
('81bcbc1f-5a01-50e5-b48e-c30622ae3a3a'::uuid, $dq$["nearMiss"]$dq$::jsonb, $dq$medium$dq$, '2026-05-16'::date, '23:30'::time, '9a0b7ef4-e0cc-5ab7-84e3-104a59e051b4'::uuid, $dq$Fossvogur$dq$, 'e1b00e7b-a5d1-5a44-a9e6-b54fc33056a3'::uuid, $dq$Zest 1$dq$, $dq$Bjarki H. sailing with single reef. Had capsized outside Nauthólsvík, stuck in mud, gone to shore. ÞA went to ramp, made contact. BH called dad who brought him back to Ýmir. ÞA had a chance to speak with him. SDS called Írís out on prammi from rowing lesson (ÞA sailed in, they came out together). ÞA righted boat.$dq$, $dq$Bjarki Hinriks; ÞA; Írís Björk; SDS$dq$, $dq$$dq$, $dq$back to house; warmed up; ÞA talked with Hinrik$dq$, $dq$SDS check in with family$dq$, $dq$guardian$dq$, $dq$Hinrik$dq$, $dq$$dq$, ARRAY[]::text[], $dq$steve$dq$, '2026-05-16T15:43:45.357Z'::timestamptz, true, '2026-05-16T15:43:45.357Z'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, $dq$closed$dq$),
('545f52bb-f87d-54d3-8a21-2cdc61327973'::uuid, $dq$["injury"]$dq$::jsonb, $dq$low$dq$, '2026-06-16'::date, '09:40'::time, 'b01b0bb1-b2f3-5276-aea0-4be1186d18ab'::uuid, $dq$Naustavör$dq$, NULL, $dq$$dq$, $dq$Staff member fell through gap in new dock finger on southwest corner while helping kids with árabátar. Superficial injury to hip as of a couple hours after. (~11:30). Mobile, active.$dq$, $dq$AK$dq$, $dq$SDS, SAB$dq$, $dq$None.$dq$, $dq$Monitor for swelling, changes$dq$, $dq$$dq$, $dq$$dq$, $dq$$dq$, ARRAY[]::text[], $dq$steve$dq$, '2026-06-16T11:26:11.555Z'::timestamptz, true, '2026-07-08T10:02:28.739Z'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, $dq$closed$dq$),
('9f539132-2eca-5d99-a7aa-ca3c068fcb7d'::uuid, $dq$["injury"]$dq$::jsonb, $dq$low$dq$, '2026-06-23'::date, '11:00'::time, '9a0b7ef4-e0cc-5ab7-84e3-104a59e051b4'::uuid, $dq$Fossvogur$dq$, '80c927e3-9a5a-596c-9461-425ac2b41666'::uuid, $dq$Terhi 1$dq$, $dq$Cut/crush injury to right thumb$dq$, $dq$Katrín Rós$dq$, $dq$$dq$, $dq$$dq$, $dq$Went to slýsó$dq$, $dq$guardian$dq$, $dq$$dq$, $dq$$dq$, ARRAY[]::text[], $dq$steve$dq$, '2026-06-24T08:59:33.670Z'::timestamptz, true, '2026-06-24T08:59:33.670Z'::timestamptz, NULL, NULL, $dq$closed$dq$),
('a1fe26d5-2999-55af-99fa-2a3f8dbf6dac'::uuid, $dq$["injury"]$dq$::jsonb, $dq$high$dq$, '2026-06-26'::date, '11:00'::time, 'b01b0bb1-b2f3-5276-aea0-4be1186d18ab'::uuid, $dq$Naustavör$dq$, NULL, $dq$$dq$, $dq$Two students fell through the remaining open triangular gap on the northwest dock corner. One (Kristinn Haukur) had leg trapped, fell backward into the water and ingested seawater. Reported having blacked out ("like a movie") at medical interview. X-ray showed no sign of water in lungs. Staff response was evidently slow; magnitude of event was unclear. Other (Ísabella Dilja) was not injured.$dq$, $dq$Kristinn Haukur Fjóluson (3110142340); Ísabella Diljá (2302142390), ÓOP$dq$, $dq$$dq$, $dq$Kristinn: Staff member ÓOP reported to SDS just after incident, but did not express seriousness of fall/difference between the two.  SDS didn't ask follow-ups about injury, only sent email reminder to City about fixing remaining gap. Parent took child to ER on way home after learning directly from them what had happened. Medical interview revealed blackout, ingestion. but X ray showed no aspiration. Parent then contacted BFG later in the day. SDS called guardian, talked through the event. Encouraged student to come back, also make sure to monitor over coming days for anxiety/psychological effects. SDS made clear that arrangements would be made if counseling, etc, is indicated. Staff met after learning of incident: nearly all had been unaware. Discussed importance of communicating full report & not having first contact with guardian be from student. SDS needs to remember to interrogate.
